༢༡

In addition to Royal Bhutan Police Act, a police personnel shall:

༡) Protect the victim and ensure that further violence is not perpetrated;

༢) Investigate the domestic violence and refer for the prosecution as per the existing laws;

༣) Aid or assist in obtaining shelter, medical treatment or any other services or measures deemed appropriate for the victim;

༤) Advice the victim of his or her right under this Act; and

༥) Take statement of the victim by the police personnel of preferably the same sex.

༢༢

If the offence is of misdemeanor and below, and the defendant is not a recidivist, a police personnel may release the defendant on surety if detained or may allow the matter to be settled mutually if the victim so desires, considering:

